{"title":"2018 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle has a chord of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the distance from the center of the circle to the chord is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of the circle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/54227df9b2bd1786f564a7d299e24ed2a7f4807b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }25\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }50\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }75\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }100\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }125\\pi \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"471\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> be the chord, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f694ab8315c055ae7dd5d9fe5ba57a1a7c97a99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> as shown below.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a98a012a46954b990fd2592abb76aa48f7e6cef5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(200); pair O, A, B, M; O = (0,0); A = (-5,5); B = (5,5); M = midpoint(A--B);  draw(Circle(O,5sqrt(2)));  dot(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, 1.5*S, linewidth(4.5)); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, 1.5*NW, linewidth(4.5)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, 1.5*NE, linewidth(4.5)); dot(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, 1.5*N, linewidth(4.5)); draw(A--B^^M--O^^A--O^^M--O^^B--O); label(&quot;$5$&quot;, midpoint(A--M), 1.5*N); label(&quot;$5$&quot;, midpoint(B--M), 1.5*N); label(&quot;$5$&quot;, midpoint(O--M), 1.5*E); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, midpoint(O--A), 1.5*SW); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, midpoint(O--B), 1.5*SE); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"335\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b28326eab546f9014a52a4e0f9bfbbdf3f0576e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OM}\\perp\\overline{AB}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/90064472691e89b8fa5d346d164022b10a189db6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM=AM=BM=5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" /> we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/d/47d8720cc891188cc83f7032ea5cba0f1fd31a19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OMA$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f56c6b549f1e7be150552138f1562aa03ded184b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OMB$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> are congruent isosceles right triangles. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba13bce93c8c157908c98da0f4cad5205e4412be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=5\\sqrt2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"23\" /> so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/38603fc90d36fae6cd305ed544feb7da08be7fdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }50\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"129\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/bJvXMkwjrtE\">https://youtu.be/bJvXMkwjrtE</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12B\" title=\"2018 AMC 12B\">2018 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a hre